{
  "_doc": [
    "Input / output pairs of Pillow's LANCZOS (Image.resize(size, Image.LANCZOS)) (generated by tools/export-recipes/wan/lanczos_fixture.py).",
    "The source of truth for the resize of the Wan2.2 I2V preprocessing (the official crop and the diffusers stretch); the TS side copies the 22-bit fixed point of Pillow's Resample.c verbatim and matches it exactly in uint8.",
    "The pixels are the U8 tensors of lanczos.safetensors: `<name>.input` [height, width, 3] and `<name>.resized` [outHeight, outWidth, 3] (RGB8, row-major).",
    "row-* / column-* sweep the production 1-D coefficient tables (832 → 1280 / 2219 / 277; 480 → 738 / 1280 / 160 / 704) with one row / one column of high-frequency noise (what is compared is the uint8 output — a ±1 in an integer coefficient shows in the output only when the multiply-accumulate crosses a 2^22 boundary, so this is no evidence that the coefficient tables match).",
    "The values depend on the Pillow version — regenerate after changing it (the recipe's wan/tests/test_lanczos_fixture.py checks them against the installed Pillow)."
